[2026-11-25] rc:4693237906 inline on src/netaddress.cpp by vasild (member) (edited 2026-11-25):
There are two things here: 1. values for `m_net` that should never be set and 2. ensure that the switch handles all enum values.

For example here there are two asserts to handle each one of 1. and 2.:

https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/edcac28380bbb8409988583b9f1ab32c41f52cac/src/netaddress.cpp#L487-L501

and here just 1. is checked:

https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/edcac28380bbb8409988583b9f1ab32c41f52cac/src/netaddress.cpp#L111-L136

The new code I added is like in the second example, handling only 1. To handle 2. one must conclude every `case` with a `return` so that the assert after the switch becomes unreachable. This is omitted in places where some work has to be done after the switch.
[2026-11-25] rc:4694470459 inline on src/netaddress.cpp by maflcko (member):
If you want to add the assert, it would be possible with a lambda, but up to you:

```cpp
enum class Tabs {
    info,
    console,
};

int GetInt(Tabs tab)
{
    int ret = [&]() {
        switch (tab) {
        case Tabs::info: return 0;
        case Tabs::console: return 1;
        } // no default case, so the compiler can warn about missing cases
        AssertUnreachable();
    }();
    LogInfo("Tab %s", ret);
    return ret;
}
```
